{"body":"Parent: #1
Depends on: #2, #3, #4

## Normative status

```text
parentClosureAuthority=web#1
decisionAuthority=false
runtimeEffects=false
legacyDeletionAuthorized=false
historicalParity=BLOCKED_SOURCE_NOT_RECOVERED
wildcardDeletionForbidden=true
```

## Purpose

Resolve the historical `specs-main/packages/jsonl-surface-lib-proof` uncertainty without inventing evidence, then make exact Astro retirement possible only after the selected `web-publication` proof is complete and recoverable.

This Issue is not “delete Astro everywhere.” It owns inventory, exact comparison or active-absence proof, deletion manifest, and rollback evidence for confirmed consumers only.

## Scope-to-meta contribution

| Level | Contribution |
|---|---|
| Scope | Identify the actual historical source and current references. |
| Quality | Prevent a replacement from claiming parity with unavailable or reconstructed evidence. |
| Architecture | Remove obsolete framework ownership only after the framework-neutral product is selected. |
| Transfer | Preserve exact rollback bytes/digests and make every deletion reviewable. |
| Meta | Reduce hidden legacy liability without destroying historical evidence or unrelated assets. |

## Known historical assertion to verify

A prior command/evidence path referred to:

```text
specs-main/packages/jsonl-surface-lib-proof
npm run prove
```

and cleaned an `.astro` directory after execution. This is an assertion to verify against exact source/history, not sufficient deletion authority.

## Required organization inventory

Search all accessible active repositories, default branches, open branches/PRs, workflows, package manifests, Nix inputs, command registries, docs, and CI intent for at least:

- `jsonl-surface-lib-proof`;
- `specs-main` path references;
- `astro`, `@astrojs/*`, `astro.config.*`;
- `.astro` source files;
- `astro dev`, `astro build`, `astro preview`;
- old archive/package names and known proof digests;
- consumers of the historical output or command.

Record results in `webPublication.legacyInventory.v1.jsonl` with repository, ref, exact path, blob/commit SHA, candidate kind, consumer relation, active status, and evidence source.

## Valid closure route A — exact historical source recovered

Recovery must include:

- exact package source;
- lockfile;
- fixtures/canonical input;
- original command and expected checks;
- exact source/archive/commit digest.

Then:

1. execute the old proof unchanged in a pinned environment;
2. capture a semantic snapshot of route set, canonicals, language, titles, heading outlines, visible text, crawlable links, citation identities/source routes, HTMX attributes and browser behavior;
3. execute the selected `web-publication` proof from the same canonical input;
4. require 100% parity for the agreed semantic fields or record exact accepted deltas through ADRS;
5. select the replacement exact commit and receipts;
6. create an exact deletion manifest;
7. delete only ready candidates;
8. prove the rollback archive restores and reruns the historical proof.

## Valid closure route B — source unavailable and no active surface

If exact source cannot be recovered:

1. complete the organization inventory;
2. prove the selected active `web-publication` package has zero Astro dependency/source/command;
3. prove no active command or package points to the retired `specs-main` path;
4. remove only confirmed stale active references;
5. preserve historical mentions that are clearly marked evidence/history;
6. record:

```text
historicalParity=NOT_CLAIMED_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
```

No reconstructed source may be represented as the historical implementation, and no semantic identity claim may be made.

## Exact deletion manifest

Each `webPublication.legacyDeletionCandidate.v1` row must include:

- candidate ID;
- repository and exact ref/path;
- current blob/commit SHA;
- candidate kind;
- active consumer count and list;
- replacement path and exact commit;
- replacement proof/readiness/bundle digests;
- rollback source and digest;
- status: `blocked`, `ready`, `deleted`, or `retained-history`;
- blocking reason;
- deletion PR and resulting readback SHA.

Glob-only or repository-name-only deletion is forbidden.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Organization-wide active inventory is reproducible and digest-pinned.
- [ ] Historical source is either recovered exactly or explicitly unavailable.
- [ ] Route A or Route B is completed without mixing their claims.
- [ ] No parity is claimed from inferred/reconstructed source.
- [ ] Selected `web-publication` proof is green before any deletion.
- [ ] Active canonical package has zero Astro dependency/source/command.
- [ ] Active retired `spec`/`specs` command references are zero.
- [ ] Every candidate has exact consumers, replacement evidence, and rollback digest.
- [ ] Unrelated repositories such as standalone Astro experiments are unchanged unless a direct active consumer relation is proven.
- [ ] Deleted candidates are absent on the exact post-effect SHA.
- [ ] Rollback bytes can restore the exact historical item independently.
- [ ] `webPublication.legacyRetirementReceipt.v1` records route, inventory digest, selected replacement, deletions, retained history, and residuals.

## Destructive cases

- wildcard deletion request;
- deleting by repository name alone;
- deleting before replacement proof/readiness receipts exist;
- consumer count omitted or stale;
- reconstructed source labeled historical original;
- Route B claiming semantic parity;
- unrelated `astroui`, `monorepo_astro`, or other experiment removed without direct consumer proof;
- rollback digest missing or not restorable;
- active command still pointing to retired path after claimed closure;
- historical evidence silently reactivated as authority.

## Non-goals

- deleting all Astro usage in the organization;
- deleting unrelated archived/experimental repositories;
- deciding the accepted framework policy independently of ADRS;
- deployment;
- final parent #1 closure by this Issue alone.

## Merge/effect condition

Inventory and proof work may merge before deletion. Any deletion PR additionally requires:

- the accepted ADRS decision/digest authorizing the exact retirement boundary;
- selected replacement commit and green receipts;
- exact candidate manifest;
- explicit human approval for those exact file/ref effects;
- post-effect readback and rollback evidence."}

