{"body":"## Purpose

Add the already-proved Vim9 conceal + text-property virtual-text extension as an edits-owned pull request.

The raw buffer remains authoritative. JSONL maps change presentation only.

```text
raw buffer
  -> JSONL: one complete map per physical line
  -> reduce by id
  -> conceal matched raw display
  -> place icon, emoji, or replacement text as virtual text
```

## Scope

- Vim9 script extension in `edits`;
- UTF-8 JSONL with one complete map per line;
- last row for the same `id` wins;
- `id`, Vim `pattern`, and `display` fields;
- optional `enabled` and `priority` fields;
- single-glyph icons, emoji, and multi-character replacement strings;
- load, reapply, and clear commands;
- real Vim proof fixtures and CI.

## Required proof

- five input rows reduce to four effective maps;
- four raw matches produce four conceal matches and four virtual-text properties;
- the screen shows role, package, and datetime replacements;
- raw `ceo` remains present and searchable;
- writing without edits leaves the content SHA-256 unchanged;
- clearing removes the added matches and properties;
- Linux and Windows real Vim headless proofs pass;
- Linux real-terminal screen output proves the visible replacements.

## Boundary

This issue owns editor presentation only.

It does not parse or lower hq multi-line command objects, define command vocabulary, write queues, create accepted identities, select providers, or execute targets. `hq#96` and `hq#112` remain the owners of command-object meaning and canonical submission.

Refs:

- `roccho-dev/hq#96`
- `roccho-dev/hq#112`
- `roccho-dev/edits#66`

## Done

- implementation PR is attached to this issue;
- repository-owned Vim9 script, JSONL maps, raw fixture, headless proof, real-screen proof, and Linux/Windows workflow are present;
- CI is green;
- removing the extension changes appearance only.
"}

