Parent: #1
Depends on: #2, #3

## Normative status

```text
parentClosureAuthority=web#1
decisionAuthority=false
runtimeEffects=false
externalIndexingClaim=false
scaleFixturePublishable=false
generatedArtifactsAreAuthority=false
```

## Purpose

Close the evidence gap between “files can be generated” and “`web-publication` is a reusable, discovery-ready product.” Separate human-reviewed publication quality from generated scale, execute browser behavior, and make all product claims fail closed.

## Scope-to-meta contribution

| Level | Contribution |
|---|---|
| Scope | Turn the local pre-proof into repeatable positive and destructive CI evidence. |
| Product | Prove the package works as a real publication compiler, not just a file generator. |
| Quality | Enforce semantic initial HTML, sources, links, canonicals, citations, fallback behavior, and content admission. |
| Scale | Prove 5,000+ pages and large relation/citation topology without confusing scale with quality. |
| Transfer | Allow any reviewer to reproduce the exact receipts from a clean checkout. |
| Meta | Convert performance and quality claims into auditable company assets. |

## Proof split

### Curated quality fixture

Use a small, human-reviewed, domain-neutral fixture. Every admitted page must have:

- one explicit page intent;
- one unique route and canonical;
- one primary H1;
- meaningful visible initial HTML before client JavaScript;
- supported factual content and traceable sources where claims are made;
- crawlable internal `a[href]` relations;
- zero exact normalized-content duplicates;
- a path from the publication root;
- valid JavaScript-free navigation and citation fallback.

Only this fixture may emit `discoveryReadiness=PASS`.

### Generated scale fixture

Must reproduce or exceed:

- 5,000 content pages;
- 100 source pages;
- 10,000 relation edges;
- 5,000 citations;
- 5,000 citation fragments;
- zero broken links;
- zero orphan pages;
- zero unresolved fragment targets;
- zero duplicate routes and canonicals;
- two clean builds with the same root digest.

It must carry:

```text
proofOnly=true
publishableContentClaim=false
discoveryReadiness=NOT_CLAIMED
```

## Required browser proof

Serve the built artifact over HTTP and execute a headless browser to prove:

1. representative full page loads;
2. primary content is visible before client JavaScript;
3. citation action triggers the expected HTMX request;
4. expected HTML fragment is inserted into the declared target;
5. normal crawlable/fallback citation link remains valid;
6. history-visible/direct-load routes return complete documents;
7. browser console has no blocking error;
8. JavaScript disabled still leaves the core document and navigation usable.

## Readiness checks

For every curated admitted page verify at least:

- valid document/media type and language;
- unique title, H1, route, and canonical;
- `main` and semantic content structure;
- visible text above a configured minimum without keyword stuffing metrics becoming authority;
- source/citation resolution;
- crawlable internal links;
- no orphan status;
- no exact normalized-content duplicate;
- no raw JSON/debug/proof UI in the canonical page;
- no required client renderer for primary content;
- renderer/body/final-file digest chain.

## Required destructive cases

At least the following must fail closed:

1. duplicate route;
2. duplicate canonical;
3. dangling internal relation;
4. orphan admitted page;
5. missing citation source;
6. unsafe/path-traversal route;
7. unsupported semantic component;
8. missing primary H1;
9. raw HTML injection;
10. Astro dependency/command/`.astro` source reintroduction;
11. active retired `specs-main` reference;
12. output manifest tampering;
13. duplicate normalized curated content;
14. scale fixture claiming readiness;
15. provider credential/SDK entering the package;
16. generated output represented as authority;
17. HTMX target missing or fragment media type wrong;
18. direct-load route returning only a fragment;
19. renderer digest mismatch;
20. same-input rebuild changing root digest.

## Evidence outputs

- `webPublication.proofReceipt.v1.json`;
- `webPublication.discoveryReadinessReceipt.v1.json`;
- browser runtime report;
- destructive-test report;
- exact fixture/input/renderer/build/output digests;
- `MANIFEST.sha256`;
- CI/Nix artifacts containing generated output, not committed `dist`.

Receipts should record duration, file count, output bytes, and peak memory where available, but one machine's timing must not become universal pass authority.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Curated fixture is human-reviewable and contains no customer-specific core implementation.
- [ ] Curated fixture readiness findings are zero.
- [ ] Scale thresholds are met or exceeded.
- [ ] Scale fixture cannot claim publishable quality/readiness.
- [ ] All links, routes, canonicals, citations, sources, fragments, and orphans are checked.
- [ ] HTMX behavior runs in a real browser, not only static attribute inspection.
- [ ] JavaScript-free core reading/navigation works.
- [ ] Two deleted-output clean builds produce the same root digest.
- [ ] All required destructive cases pass by rejecting the broken fixture.
- [ ] Generated output remains artifact-only and non-authority.
- [ ] One command from a clean checkout produces all selected receipts.

## Non-goals

- public deployment;
- Search Console/Bing/AI citation observation;
- ranking or revenue guarantees;
- historical Astro parity/deletion;
- ADRS acceptance or governance final join;
- parent #1 closure.

## Merge condition

Merge only when curated quality, scale, browser, JavaScript-free fallback, deterministic rebuild, and destructive proof receipts are all green on the exact candidate SHA. A 5,000-file count alone is not sufficient.

