state.body:
Parent: #1
Depends on: #2, #3, #4
Cross-repo dependencies: `roccho-dev/adrs#244`, `roccho-dev/ui#146`, `roccho-dev/governance#167`
Legacy evidence dependency: #5

## Normative status

```text
parentClosureAuthority=web#1
decisionAuthority=false
runtimeEffects=false
physicalDeploymentOutOfScope=true
organizationActiveClaim=false
generatedArtifactsAreAuthority=false
```

## Purpose

Turn the implemented `web-publication` product into exact, replayable package claims and receipts consumable by governance and due diligence. Ensure clean-checkout reconstruction, exact candidate-SHA evidence, provider-neutral release output, and explicit residuals before parent closure.

## Scope-to-meta contribution

| Level | Contribution |
|---|---|
| Scope | Wire the selected product checks and artifacts into one reproducible package/CI entrypoint. |
| Product | Make the actual package claim its identity, renderer, quality, scale, framework, and bundle state. |
| Governance | Bind every claim to the accepted ADRS digest and exact candidate SHA. |
| Transfer | Prove a third party can delete outputs and rebuild/inspect the product from pinned inputs. |
| Business | Expose measurable product evidence without treating generated sites as source authority. |
| Meta | Reduce diligence, migration, and hidden-dependency risk in the Web product asset. |

## Preconditions

Before organization-active claims or parent closure:

- `adrs#244` must have an accepted validated decision record and exact digest;
- #2 core/bundle contract must be merged;
- `ui#146` and #3 must provide/pin the selected renderer and digest;
- #4 proof/readiness/browser/determinism receipts must be green;
- #5 must provide exact legacy status, even if historical parity remains explicitly unavailable/blocked;
- `governance#167` must define the accepted package-facing obligations.

Fixture/shadow work may precede ADRS acceptance only if clearly marked non-authority and blocked from final claims.

## Required package claims

Emit `webPublication.packageClaim.v1` pinned to:

- repository and package identity;
- accepted ADRS decision ID/version/digest;
- exact candidate commit SHA;
- public contract versions/digests;
- selected UI renderer repository/revision/output digest;
- external canonical input digest;
- curated readiness receipt digest;
- scale proof receipt digest;
- browser/fallback receipt digest;
- deterministic bundle root digest;
- dependency/lock/license inventory digest;
- framework findings;
- deprecated path findings;
- legacy retirement route/status/receipt digest;
- residuals and next actions;
- `generatedArtifactsAreAuthority:false`.

Claims must not state ranking, indexing, AI citation, traffic, revenue, deployment, or company sale outcomes.

## Required receipt outputs

At minimum:

```text
webPublication.packageClaim.v1.jsonl
webPublication.proofReceipt.v1.json
webPublication.discoveryReadinessReceipt.v1.json
webPublication.browserReceipt.v1.json
webPublication.determinismReceipt.v1.json
webPublication.dependencyReceipt.v1.json
webPublication.legacyRetirementReceipt.v1.json
webPublication.bundle.v1.json
MANIFEST.sha256
```

If governance selects generic company-wide receipt kinds, package-local compatibility aliases must not create a second meaning authority.

## Nix/package and CI surface

Provide one pinned, non-interactive selected proof entrypoint that:

1. starts from declared external JSONL and exact renderer input;
2. builds the curated and scale proofs;
3. runs semantic/network/destructive/browser checks;
4. performs a deleted-output clean double build;
5. emits the provider-neutral bundle and all receipts;
6. verifies manifest/root digests;
7. packages generated pages as CI/Nix artifacts only;
8. returns nonzero on any missing/stale/unknown input or finding.

Declare every provider workflow in `ci.intent.v1.jsonl`. Provider YAML is an adapter artifact, not authority.

## Clean-checkout transfer proof

From a clean checkout at the exact candidate SHA:

- install/build only from pinned/declared dependencies;
- delete all generated output and caches;
- execute the selected proof using documented commands;
- reproduce all required receipts and bundle root digest;
- show no untracked source/config is required;
- show no credentials/network deployment effects are required;
- record environment/toolchain identity without making one host authoritative;
- provide a reviewer readback explaining owner boundaries and how to rebuild.

## Required findings and fail-closed behavior

Fail when:

- ADRS claim digest is proposed/missing/stale;
- candidate SHA differs from receipt target;
- renderer revision/output digest differs;
- any required proof/readiness/browser/determinism receipt is absent or stale;
- scale fixture claims readiness;
- external outcome claims appear;
- generated output is tracked or described as authority;
- Astro is required by the selected proof;
- deprecated `spec`/`specs` path remains active;
- provider SDK/credential/deploy state enters the package;
- dependency lock/license inventory is absent;
- legacy status is omitted or parity overclaimed;
- clean checkout cannot reproduce the bundle root digest;
- governance package response omits `web-publication` or its required receipt set.

## Governance handoff

Expose a repo/package evidence packet consumable by `governance#167`, containing:

- package inventory;
- exact claim rows;
- required receipt references and digests;
- provider CI state/intent;
- findings/residuals;
- non-authority manifest;
- candidate SHA and accepted ADRS digest.

Governance readback must distinguish:

```text
package proof green
!= organization-active
```

No branch-protection/cutover effect is part of this Issue.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] One documented selected proof command emits all required artifacts.
- [ ] All claims bind accepted decision digest and exact candidate SHA.
- [ ] Package/renderer/input/output/dependency/legacy digests form a traceable chain.
- [ ] Generated pages are artifact-only and can be fully deleted/rebuilt.
- [ ] Clean-checkout proof reproduces the selected bundle root digest.
- [ ] No credentials, provider deployment, or external outcome claims occur.
- [ ] CI intent and workflow behavior are aligned and tested.
- [ ] Governance consumes the packet and reports exact residuals/next actions.
- [ ] Local green is not represented as final organization-active authority.
- [ ] A third-party reviewer can identify all owners and rerun evidence without Issue prose as hidden input.

## Non-goals

- physical deployment or hosting;
- branch protection/cutover;
- Search Console/Bing/AI observation;
- acceptance of `adrs#244`;
- renderer implementation;
- historical deletion effects;
- parent #1 closure without final human review.

## Merge condition

Merge only after exact accepted ADRS input is available for final claims, or keep pre-acceptance work fixture/shadow-only. The final PR must have green selected proof, exact candidate-SHA receipts, clean-checkout reproduction, dependency/license receipt, governance packet readback, and no hidden residuals.

## Closure contribution

This Issue is complete when the package evidence is selected and consumable. Parent #1 remains open until all child Issues, legacy status, exact PR SHAs/digests, residuals, and explicit human closure approval are recorded.

