### Governance workflows

End state: exactly two active governance workflow surfaces.

#### 1. `gov-gate`

The stable required check identity remains:

```text
gov-final-scope-purpose-join / gate
```

The workflow may retain or migrate the existing filename, but the check-name cutover must be explicit and read back.

Required jobs or equivalent isolated stages:

| Stage | Responsibility | Write secrets | Candidate code execution |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| `capture` | read and seal accepted ADRS source, feature claim, receipt registry, engine contract, and candidate SHA | none | no |
| `regression` | run engine/schema/selftests and destructive fixtures when relevant | none | governance code only |
| `materialize` | normalize inputs and produce canonical digests | none | no |
| `evaluate` | run current claim join, admission, code rules, and scope/package/purpose closure | none | only inside a secret-free sandbox when required |
| `gate` | reduce all mandatory results to one allow/block for the exact SHA | none | no |
| `evidence` | publish sealed packet, findings, and pre-effect decision | artifact/check output only | no |
| `post-effect` | read back selected ref/merge result and bind it to the pre-effect decision | bounded provider write/read as accepted | no |

