{"body":"Parent: #4

Architecture constraint: #6

Related: #2, #5

Adjacent but independent: roccho-dev/ui#116, roccho-dev/ui#117

## Current implementation state — 2026-07-26

- PR A / hosted Work View: **merged** through PR #11.
- Actual hosted Viewer open: **proven**.
- Native Edit action and official Editor entry: **proven**.
- Editor input XML digest equals the source digest: **proven**.
- PR B / self-hosted compiled official GraphViewer: **not complete**.
- Generic render-quality admission is **not owned by this Issue**. A separate render-audit Issue owns text clipping, occlusion, contrast, crossings, and deterministic render findings over a pinned runtime.
- This Issue owns only the two view products and their native behavior: hosted Work View and compiled GraphViewer.

## Purpose

Materialize one `mxGraphModel / mxfile` into two non-authoritative projections with different operating purposes:

1. **Work View**
   - open quickly in the hosted draw.io lightbox;
   - preserve native pages, layers, links, zoom and fit;
   - move directly into the official draw.io Editor;
   - apply no semantic visibility filtering.

2. **Compiled Viewer**
   - materialize the official draw.io `GraphViewer` as a self-hostable static HTML bundle;
   - change only runtime cell visibility as zoom increases;
   - preserve native draw.io rendering rather than creating a custom SVG, canvas, camera or world model.

```text
events.jsonl                    authority
      ↓
mxGraphModel / mxfile           sole generated current state
      ├─ hosted Work View       quick review + official Editor entry
      └─ compiled GraphViewer   clean read-only semantic visibility
```

This Issue does not prove corporate sale, buyer demand, enterprise value or transaction completion. It indirectly reduces explanation, transfer and maintainability risk by preserving one model and two reproducible views.

## Why this belongs under #4

#4 owns the product-facing view/edit/proof/export depth and the unresolved z-axis UX. This Issue concretizes two view modes within that boundary.

#6 remains the stronger architecture constraint:

```text
events.jsonl = authority
mxGraphModel = sole generated current state
projections / editors = consumers
```

This Issue must not reintroduce DVM, `RenderAst`, `RenderingIR`, another public IR or another current-state artifact.

## Decision

```text
one mxGraphModel
  ├─ hosted Work View
  └─ compiled official GraphViewer
```

### Fixed invariants

- `events.jsonl` remains authority.
- `mxGraphModel / mxfile` remains generated and non-authoritative.
- Work View URL is non-authoritative.
- Compiled Viewer HTML is non-authoritative.
- Runtime visibility is non-authoritative.
- Zoom must not mutate or rewrite the source model.
- Work View and Compiled Viewer must consume the exact same source digest.

## Scope

### Included

- one validated `mxfile` input;
- multi-page viewing;
- one official-compatible hosted Work View URL format;
- actual hosted-browser proof;
- official Editor entry and payload proof;
- exact pin of `viewer-static.min.js`;
- self-hostable static HTML using official `GraphViewer`;
- zoom-dependent binary cell visibility;
- preservation of native page, layer, link, pan, zoom and fit behavior;
- source digest comparison;
- real-browser runtime proof;
- deterministic bundle generation;
- destructive fixtures and fail-closed receipts;
- zero runtime external network requests for the compiled bundle.

### Excluded

- draw.io fork or source rebuild;
- full Editor self-hosting;
- custom SVG, Canvas or WebGL renderer;
- `svg-pan-zoom`;
- custom camera;
- custom world model or LOD IR;
- `context/detail/hidden` source schema;
- focus or click-driven drill-down state;
- zoom-dependent style, opacity, color or label replacement;
- edge aggregation or synthetic edges;
- semantic edit import, semantic/visual diff or event append implementation;
- hosting, DNS, domain or provider deployment;
- publication page networks;
- `ui` repository changes;
- full JS migration from #5;
- automatic tracking of the newest draw.io version;
- generic render-audit findings or visual-quality admission.

## Authority boundary

| Object | Authority |
|---|---:|
| `events.jsonl` | yes |
| `mxGraphModel / mxfile` | no |
| Work View URL | no |
| Editor runtime state | no |
| Compiled Viewer HTML | no |
| zoom visibility state | no |
| browser proof | receipt only |
| manifest | receipt only |
| render-audit receipt | evidence only; separate Issue |

## Work View contract

The merged PR A proves:

- actual hosted origin opened;
- no error dialog;
- expected page, vertex and edge counts;
- native Edit action exists;
- official Editor opened;
- Editor payload digest equals source digest;
- no custom renderer or custom JavaScript fallback.

Network or browser policy blocking this proof produces `BLOCKED`, never `PASS`.

## Compiled Viewer contract

The generated HTML is self-owned, but drawing is performed by the official `GraphViewer`.

```text
self-owned:
  HTML host
  exact XML transport
  visibility rule
  manifest
  proof

official draw.io runtime:
  shape rendering
  labels
  edges
  pages
  layers
  links
  pan
  zoom
  fit
```

### Viewer Runtime pin

Record and verify:

- exact upstream version;
- exact source URL;
- exact SHA-256;
- preserved license;
- exact `viewer-static.min.js` bytes;
- no CDN/latest dependency at runtime.

### Runtime network

The compiled bundle must satisfy:

```text
external script request: 0
external stylesheet request: 0
external font request: 0
external image auto-fetch: 0
connect-src: none
```

A source model requiring an external image is rejected in v1.

## Semantic visibility v1

```text
effectiveVisibility(cell)
  = nativeDrawioVisibility(cell)
  AND zoomDerivedVisibility(cell)
```

Use only `minScreenWidthPx` and `minScreenHeightPx` in v1. Zooming in may reveal more detail; zooming out may hide detail. Under a fixed native layer/tag/collapse state:

```text
visible(far) ⊆ visible(middle) ⊆ visible(near)
```

An edge is visible only when both endpoints are visible. V1 must not reconnect, aggregate, synthesize, truncate, or restyle edges.

The serialized source model digest before and after all zoom operations must be identical.

## Browser proof

A real browser must prove:

- official `GraphViewer` initialized;
- source digest exact;
- page count exact;
- far/middle/near visibility expected and readable;
- monotonic visibility;
- native pages, layers, links, pan, zoom and fit preserved;
- hidden-endpoint edges absent;
- model digest unchanged;
- console errors zero;
- external runtime requests zero;
- two clean builds byte-equivalent.

DOM counts alone are insufficient.

## PR split

### PR A — Work View

Status: **merged as PR #11**.

### PR B — Compiled Viewer

Starts from the latest default branch and must not stack on the active #6 cutover proof branch.

Includes:

- exact Viewer Runtime pin;
- generated HTML host;
- visibility-only extension;
- manifest;
- far/middle/near screenshots;
- external-request proof;
- deterministic rebuild proof;
- destructive fixtures.

Excludes Work URL codec changes, full Editor, event append, custom renderer, render-audit policy, and `ui` changes.

## Current evidence status

```text
hosted Work View actual open             PASS
official Editor entry                    PASS
Editor input digest parity               PASS
compiled GraphViewer implementation      NOT_RUN
pinned render-quality audit              separate Issue
```

## Close conditions

Close only when:

- [x] Work View opens on the actual hosted origin;
- [x] Work View opens the official Editor;
- [x] Editor input digest equals source digest;
- [ ] official `GraphViewer` initializes inside the compiled bundle;
- [ ] Viewer Runtime is pinned by exact version and digest;
- [ ] runtime external requests are zero;
- [ ] far/middle/near visibility is proven visually;
- [ ] visible cells grow monotonically with zoom;
- [ ] native page/layer/link behavior is preserved;
- [ ] hidden-endpoint edges are absent;
- [ ] model digest remains unchanged after zoom;
- [ ] two clean builds are byte-equivalent;
- [ ] all destructive fixtures fail as expected;
- [ ] custom SVG/canvas/world/LOD IR count is zero;
- [ ] exact-head and merge-ref CI are green;
- [ ] merged `proposals` readback preserves one source digest for both views."}

