{"body":"Refs #2
Relates #12, #19

## Problem

The source contract correctly says:

```text
proposals = canonical/default/PR base
main      = retained compatibility branch
main direct change = forbidden by contract
effect source       = proposals only
```

The repository checker also rejects an invalid `main` refresh: on a `main` push it requires `HEAD == fetched proposals`.

However, current GitHub branch-protection readback reports protection disabled. Therefore:

```text
source contract says "forbidden"
!= GitHub repository physically prevents unauthorized update
```

This is a repository-administration readiness gap, not a source-code failure.

## Goal

Make GitHub repository rules enforce the accepted branch authority without introducing continuous `proposals -> main` synchronization.

## Required outcome

### proposals

- remains default/canonical/PR base;
- normal changes require the accepted PR path;
- required repository check is enforced;
- force/delete paths are not silently available to normal writers.

### main

- remains present and noncanonical;
- no ordinary direct development;
- compatibility refresh is an explicit bounded operation;
- every refresh still requires the post-update exact-equality check against then-current `proposals`;
- no continuous synchronization claim is introduced.

The exact GitHub mechanism may be branch protection or a repository ruleset. Prefer one small repository-native mechanism.

## Fail-closed readback

```text
SOURCE_BRANCH_POLICY = PASS
PHYSICAL_BRANCH_ENFORCEMENT = NO while this Issue is open
```

Do not promote the source policy to physical enforcement PASS.

## Done

- [ ] current ruleset/protection configuration is read back;
- [ ] canonical `proposals` update path is physically constrained;
- [ ] ordinary direct development on `main` is physically constrained;
- [ ] explicit compatibility refresh remains possible;
- [ ] `main` post-refresh equality check remains Green;
- [ ] force/delete/bypass behavior and authorized bypass actors, if any, are recorded non-secretly;
- [ ] #2 records physical branch enforcement PASS only after readback.

## Non-goals

- deleting `main`;
- continuously syncing `main`;
- making `main` canonical;
- using branch protection as provider-effect evidence."}

