## Purpose

Close the execution gap discovered after PR #166: an owner-controlled helper can dispatch `gov-release`, but GitHub records the resulting workflow actor as `github-actions[bot]`, so the existing direct-owner actor check correctly blocks publication.

Preserve the accepted ADRS #242 meaning and add the smallest transport adapter that proves owner authorization without putting provider metadata into the release manifest.

## Required behavior

`gov-release` may proceed when either:

1. `github.actor == github.repository_owner` on `refs/heads/proposals`; or
2. the actor is `github-actions[bot]` and the workflow receives an exact owner-authored authorization comment ID.

The referenced comment must:

- be authored by the repository owner;
- contain one closed canonical JSON object;
- bind exact release ID, sequence, previous/supersedes digest, governance engine SHA and accepted-decision digest;
- have `status=approved`;
- have no meaning authority and no business/all-repository claim.

## Evidence boundary

- comment ID, actor and provider metadata belong only to `gov-release-owner-authorization-transport.json` and the release readback receipt;
- the canonical `govReleaseManifest.v1` must remain unchanged;
- publisher still must not checkout or execute candidate code;
- direct owner dispatch remains supported;
- no new workflow is added.

## Acceptance

- exact owner comment positive fixture passes;
- wrong author, wrong engine SHA, wrong decision digest, wrong release inputs, malformed/extra fields and unapproved status are rejected;
- authorization transport bytes are included in evaluated/published assets and post-publication readback;
- stable gate/Nix/live consumer checks remain green;
- permanent workflow count remains three;
- expected-head merge and default readback complete.

## Closure boundary

This Issue closes only the owner-authorization transport adapter. Actual sequence-0 gov release publication, canary selected-state readback and #223/#150/#233 closure follow immediately afterward.

## Purpose

Close the DRY defect in Governance PR #166 without changing the accepted gov-release architecture.

The same exact ADRS identity is currently repeated across PR text, workflows, Python constants, baseline JSON and `ci.intent`. This already caused stale references (`60dcc0bd...` versus current ADRS PR #242 head `5a8a6d99...`) and makes false-green or false-red drift possible.

## Required result

Create exactly one checked-in, non-authority identity projection containing:

- ADRS repository and PR number;
- exact ADRS candidate/accepted head;
- accepted-decision bundle canonical digest;
- gov-release contract canonical digest;
- stable gate name;
- transitional current accepted merge;
- decision status;
- `allRepositoriesEnforced=false` and business outcome false.

All Governance workflows and checkers must read this projection. They must not independently hard-code the ADRS head or the two release digests.

## Scope

- base the implementation on PR #166 branch `feat/150-gov-release-adoption`;
- update gate, canary and release workflows to load identity values through step outputs;
- update Python checkers and baseline validation to read the projection;
- keep GitHub/provider identifiers out of release meaning;
- update the validated UI receipt snapshot to the current exact-head artifact;
- remove `.github/workflows/tmp-live-consumer-metadata.yml`;
- retain exactly three permanent workflows: gate, canary, release;
- update PR #166 description after the child PR merges.

## Non-goals

- no new decision authority;
- no signature, key, promotion-chain or ruleset mechanism;
- no additional workflow surface;
- no production gov release publication in this child PR;
- no all-repository or business-outcome claim.

## Acceptance

1. One identity projection is the only checked-in source for ADRS head, accepted-decision digest and release-contract digest.
2. Static tests reject duplicate literal copies outside the projection and its tests/fixtures.
3. Current UI evidence is exact:
   - head `6b67ceb865de7f6a0318eb5a5eeb83af8567b21b`
   - run `29669921169`
   - artifact `8436961170`
   - artifact digest `sha256:388731ff417f064e7356b3b21ee9ba6d4bb2022f1adfcbb100bf1422da0b48e5`
   - ZIP receipt `candidateSha` equals the head.
4. Temporary metadata workflow is absent.
5. Workflow count is exactly three.
6. Exact child-PR head passes ADRS source capture, live UI/Ops receipt capture, Nix regression, gov-release tests and stable gate.
7. Merge is expected-head guarded and read back.

## Closure boundary

Closing this Issue proves DRY and exact-identity integration on PR #166's candidate branch. It does not close #150/#223/#233 and does not claim operational adoption; actual gov-release publication and readback remain required later.

