## Parent

Parent: governance #125
Phase parent: governance #82

This issue is complete only if its output contributes to selected real package `closure-pass`.
`handoff-ready`, `report-generated`, artifact output, drift rows, and work-order rows are not pass.

## Purpose

Cut over the selected branch/ref merge-write boundary so `gov-final-scope-purpose-join / gate` is the effective merge authority.

GitHub ruleset / branch protection is one valid implementation path, but it is not required. A self-hosted git server gate, server-side hook, merge daemon, bot-only merge path, or SSOT publish gate is also valid if it proves the same enforcement property.

## Core rule

CI green is not enough.

This issue closes only when the selected branch/ref cannot be updated unless the final gate accepts the exact target commit SHA.

## Post-merge state

After attached PRs or external enforcement evidence are accepted:

- the selected branch/ref write boundary is protected by the final gate;
- `gov-final-scope-purpose-join / gate` is the effective required gate name;
- old CI, artifact exporters, shadow reports, and handoff helpers do not provide independent merge authority;
- rollback instructions are recorded;
- every allowed or rejected update leaves an audit receipt.

## Allowed enforcement providers

Any one of these is acceptable:

| Provider | Acceptable when |
|---|---|
| GitHub ruleset / branch protection | required status check is active for the selected branch/ref |
| self-hosted git server hook | server-side update is rejected unless final gate passes |
| merge daemon / bot-only merge | humans cannot write selected refs directly; daemon enforces final gate |
| bare repo SSOT + checked mirror publish | selected ref or mirror publish is refused without final gate receipt |

PR comments or human convention alone are not acceptable enforcement.

## Required evidence

- final gate name: `gov-final-scope-purpose-join / gate`;
- same-name green evidence for the final gate;
- enforcement point: GitHub ruleset, self-hosted hook, merge daemon, bot-only merge, or SSOT publish gate;
- reject proof: an update without final gate pass, with stale gate output, or with digest/SHA mismatch is refused;
- accept proof: the exact target SHA can be updated only after final gate pass;
- audit receipt: target SHA, gate run/check identity, decision, timestamp, and actor/path are recorded;
- rollback instructions;
- old-CI demotion evidence showing old checks are producer, artifact, selftest, or internal-step surfaces only.

## Merge blockers

Do not close this issue when:

- only CI is green but selected refs can still be updated manually;
- enforcement is only documented but not active;
- the required gate name differs from the emitted final check name;
- old CI remains a parallel merge authority;
- reject proof is missing;
- accept proof is missing;
- rollback or audit receipt is missing;
- governance is described as meaning authority.

## Boundary

This issue does not require GitHub-specific rulesets.

It does require a real merge/write boundary gate. Without such a gate, governance remains diagnostic and #125 cannot honestly reach selected real package `closure-pass`.

This issue changes enforcement/cutover only. It must not change the final gate's semantic behavior.

